        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Duke University, Tufts University\n- People: James David Barber, Donald Sur\n- Places: Durham, North Carolina, Trinity, Boston, Massachusetts\n- Topics: university founding, relocation, academic appointments\n\nFacts:\n- Duke University was founded by Methodists and Quakers in the present-day town of Trinity in 1838.\n- Tufts College was founded in 1852 by Christian Universalists who sought to create a nonsectarian institution of higher learning.\n- Duke University moved from Trinity to Durham in 1892.\n- Donald Sur received his doctorate from Harvard in 1972 and then settled in Boston, Massachusetts.\n- James David Barber taught political science at Duke University from 1977 to 1995.\n- In Boston, Donald Sur had many of his works premiered and taught at local universities including Harvard, MIT, and Tufts.\n- Duke University is a private research university located in Durham, North Carolina.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a4671490-ef3c-523d-967e-66a18b2d2d24",
        "text": "Page: Duke University. Sentence: Duke University is a private research university located in Durham, North Carolina.\nPage: Duke University. Sentence: Founded by Methodists and Quakers in the present-day town of Trinity in 1838, the school moved to Durham in 1892.\nPage: Tufts University. Sentence: Tufts College was founded in 1852 by Christian Universalists who worked for years to open a nonsectarian institution of higher learning.\nPage: James David Barber. Sentence: From 1977 to 1995, he taught political science at Duke University.\nPage: Donald Sur. Sentence: After receiving his doctorate from Harvard in 1972, he settled in Boston, Massachusetts, where many of his works were premiered and where he taught at several local universities, including Harvard, MIT, and Tufts.",
